VI  - 18
IP  - 4
DP  - 2021 Apr
TI  - Dyspnea in Chronic Low Ventricular Preload States.
PG  - 573-581
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.202005-581CME [doi]
AB  - Dyspnea in low-preload states is an underrecognized but growing diagnosis in 
      patients with unexplained dyspnea. Patients can often experience debilitating 
      symptoms at rest and with exertion, as low measured preload often leads to 
      decreased cardiac output and ultimately dyspnea. In the present article, we 
      performed a review of the literature and a multidisciplinary evaluation to 
      understand the pathophysiology, diagnosis, and treatment of dyspnea in 
      low-preload states. We explored selected etiologies and suggested an algorithm to 
      approach unexplained dyspnea. The mainstay of diagnosis remains as invasive 
      cardiopulmonary exercise testing. We concluded with a variety of 
      nonpharmacological and pharmacological therapies, highlighting that a 
      multifactorial approach may lead to the best results.
