TI  - Helper T-cell type 17 cytokines and immunity in the lung.
PG  - S284-6
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.201403-109AW [doi]
AB  - The HIV epidemic has clearly demonstrated the critical role CD4(+) T cells play 
      in preventing opportunistic infections in the lung. The types of CD4(+) effector 
      T-cell populations in the lung have significantly expanded over the last 8-10 
      years with the discovery of helper T type 17 cells, and this review summarizes 
      the field and discusses how these effector cells may be exploited to augment 
      mucosal immunity in the lung.
