TI  - Care of the Transgender Patient with a Pulmonary Complaint.
PG  - 931-937
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.202007-801CME [doi]
AB  - Individuals who identify with a gender not typically associated with their sex 
      assigned at birth are a growing population worldwide. Guidelines to help 
      healthcare providers navigate the care of gender minorities (GMs) are often aimed 
      at primary care providers and may be too general for subspecialists. 
      Pulmonologists may see GM individuals for a variety of reasons, and no reference 
      exists that contains relevant information about GM-specific care, including 
      unique conditions to consider. A systematic review was completed to identify 
      unique characteristics in caring for GM patients with a pulmonary complaint.
