TI  - Host and Viral Determinants of Respiratory Syncytial Virus-induced Airway Mucus.
PG  - S205-S209
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.201806-380AW [doi]
AB  - Respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) is a leading cause of hospitalization of 
      infants worldwide each year. Both host and viral factors host factors predispose 
      a subset of what appear to be healthy infants to severe RSV-induced disease. In 
      this review, we outline many genetic and immunologic factors that contribute to 
      airway obstruction that contributes to the severity of RSV infection.
