TI  - CEASE: a guide for clinicians on how to stop resuscitation efforts.
PG  - 440-5
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.201412-552PS [doi]
AB  - Resuscitation programs such as Advanced Cardiac Life Support, Cardiac Life 
      Support, Pediatric Advanced Life Support, and the Neonatal Resuscitation Program 
      offer inadequate guidance to physicians who must ultimately decide when to stop 
      resuscitation efforts. These decisions involve clinical and ethical judgments and 
      are complicated by communication challenges, group dynamics, and family 
      considerations. This article presents a framework, summarized in a mnemonic 
      (CEASE: Clinical Features, Effectiveness, Ask, Stop, Explain), for how to stop 
      resuscitation efforts and communicate that decision to clinicians and ultimately 
      the patient's family. Rather than a decision rule, this mnemonic represents a 
      framework based on best evidence for when physicians are considering stopping 
      resuscitation efforts and provides guidance on how to communicate that decision.
