TI  - Communicating with Congress.
PG  - 386-9
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.201305-128OT [doi]
AB  - Influencing policy to improve health can be considered an extension of health 
      care workers' duty to help people. Communicating with elected representatives is 
      a basic mechanism to effect lasting change. Communications that influence public 
      officials should be clear, concise, courteous, and logical. They are strengthened 
      by citing evidence and example. They must recommend a course of action, which 
      should be principled and related to the representative's constituents.
