TI  - A human breathing lung-on-a-chip.
PG  - S42-4
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.201410-442MG [doi]
AB  - Here we describe a microphysiological system that replicates the functional unit 
      of the living human lung. This human "breathing lung-on-a-chip" microdevice 
      provides unique capabilities to reconstitute three-dimensional microarchitecture, 
      dynamic mechanical activity, and integrated physiological function of the 
      alveolar-capillary interface. We demonstrate the potential of this 
      microengineered biomimetic model for screening environmental particulates and 
      modeling complex human disease processes.
