OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20180724
LR  - 20260726
IS  - 2325-6621 (Electronic)
IS  - 2329-6933 (Print)
IS  - 2325-6621 (Linking)
VI  - 14
IP  - Supplement_5
DP  - 2017 Nov
TI  - Pathophysiology to Phenotype in the Asthma of Obesity.
PG  - S395-S398
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.201702-122AW [doi]
AB  - Obesity affects numerous diseases, including asthma, for reasons that remain 
      incompletely understood. Recent research suggests that the asthma of obesity is 
      not a single disease, and that it breaks out into at least two distinct 
      phenotypes. One phenotype is conventional allergic asthma modulated by obesity, 
      whereas another arises solely due to the presence of obesity. The latter is 
      postulated to be a consequence of the chronic lung compression caused by the 
      obese chest wall in individuals with particularly collapsible lungs. Allergic 
      obese asthma, on the other hand, appears to result from the way that obesity 
      affects the immune system, which we hypothesize can be understood in terms of 
      effects on the dynamic regulation of the inflammatory response.
